This example program raises an error so that we can check that
[[nolinemap]] maps the traceback back to this file.

<<example.py>>=
def f():
    <<raise an error>>

print(<<the answer>>)
f()
@

The error itself lives in its own chunk.  It is a chunk of a single
line, so its splice carries no marker and anchors to the line that
uses it: the traceback should point at the use, line 6.
<<raise an error>>=
raise ValueError("expect example.nw line 6")
@

A chunk used in the middle of a line must splice cleanly, with no
marker breaking the line:
<<the answer>>=
6*7
@
